IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bda-debt-agreements`

-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) -- what bankruptcy itself would mean, as far as a debtor weighing a debt agreement needs it:
-- how long I would be bankrupt (ss 149, 149A, with s 149D's grounds of objection); what discharge releases (s 153(1), (2)); and
-- whether I would have to pay income contributions (ss 139K, 139P, 139Q), with the dependant income limit in Bankruptcy Regulations
-- 2021 s 36.
--
-- SEAT: the debtor -- here, the debtor asking "What would bankruptcy mean for me instead?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 97, compilation date 21 May 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 47, 2026), Federal Register of
-- Legislation register id C2026C00215, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1966A00033.txt. Regulations: Bankruptcy
-- Regulations 2021, Compilation No. 5, compilation date 1 July 2026 (register id F2026C00537), as deposited at
-- ../../../bankruptcy-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/F2021L00261.txt -- s 36 (income of a dependant).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the amount of a contribution -- s 139S prints "the formula:" and then none, so only whether I am liable, and by how
-- much my income exceeds the threshold, are worked out; the base income threshold amount itself (3.5 times an indexed Social
-- Security Act 1991 rate), an INPUT; the CPI indexation of the s 36 amount after 2020-21 (Regulations s 114), an INPUT; part-year
-- contribution periods; s 139L's meaning of income; hardship increases (s 139T); the grounds of objection to discharge one by one
-- (s 149D), asked as a fact; vesting of property (s 58), divisible property (s 116), the trustee's powers, and offences.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with the
-- design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use
-- as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Bankruptcy Act 1966 -- what bankruptcy would mean for me`

§§ `149, 149A -- how long I would be bankrupt`

-- s 149(1): "A bankrupt is discharged from bankruptcy, by force of this subsection, at the end of the period of 3 years from" (a) for a
-- sequestration order, "the date the statement of the bankrupt's affairs accepted under subsection 57B(1) was filed"; (b) for a
-- debtor's petition, "the date the Official Receiver accepted the debtor's petition".
-- s 149A(1), (2)(a): if an objection to discharge has taken effect, discharge is at the end of "(i) if the objection was made on a
-- ground, or on grounds that included a ground, referred to in paragraph 149D(1)(ab), (ac), (ad), (d), (da), (e), (f), (g), (h),
-- (ha), (ia), (k) or (ma) -- 8 years; or (ii) in any other case -- 5 years". (3): if the objection is withdrawn or cancelled, it "is
-- taken never to have been made".
-- Whether the trustee objects, and on which ground, is the trustee's; it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Objection to discharge` IS ONE OF
    `no objection in effect`
    `an objection on a ground listed in s 149A(2)(a)(i)`
    `an objection on another ground`

@export How many years would I stay bankrupt (ss 149, 149A)?
GIVEN `the objection` IS AN `Objection to discharge` @desc Whether your trustee has an objection to your discharge in effect, and on what kind of ground
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years would I be bankrupt` IS
    CONSIDER `the objection`
    WHEN `no objection in effect` THEN 3
    WHEN `an objection on a ground listed in s 149A(2)(a)(i)` THEN 8
    WHEN `an objection on another ground` THEN 5

@export On what day would I be discharged from bankruptcy (ss 149, 149A)?
GIVEN `the starting day` IS A NUMBER @desc For a debtor's petition, the day the Official Receiver accepted it; for a sequestration order, the day your statement of affairs was filed; as YYYYMMDD
      `the objection` IS AN `Objection to discharge` @desc Whether your trustee has an objection to your discharge in effect, and on what kind of ground
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `When would I be discharged` IS
    `the same day years later` `the starting day` (`How many years would I be bankrupt` `the objection`)

§§ `153 -- what discharge would release`

-- s 153(1): discharge "operates to release him or her from all debts (including secured debts) provable in the bankruptcy". (2) it
-- does not release "(b) a debt incurred by means of fraud" or "(c) subject to any order of the Court made under subsection (2A)" any
-- liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order. Note: a pecuniary penalty order is not provable (s 82(3A)).
-- A debt incurred after the bankruptcy is not provable in it (inference); the Debt kind for "after acceptance for processing" is
-- read here as "after the bankruptcy began".
@export If I became bankrupt, would my discharge release me from this debt (s 153)?
GIVEN `the debt` IS A `Debt kind` @desc The kind of debt ("incurred after acceptance for processing" is read as incurred after the bankruptcy began)
      `the Court ordered release from maintenance arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a maintenance liability, whether the Court ordered under s 153(2A) that discharge releases the arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would discharge release me from the debt` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `an ordinary provable debt` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a liability under a maintenance agreement or maintenance order` THEN `the Court ordered release from maintenance arrears`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `139K, 139P, 139Q -- income contributions`

-- s 139K: "actual income threshold amount" is the base income threshold amount, "(b) if the bankrupt has one dependant ... increased
-- by 18%; (c) ... 2 dependants ... 27%; (d) ... 3 dependants ... 32%; (e) ... 4 dependants ... 34%; (f) ... more than 4 dependants
-- ... 36%". "base income threshold amount" for a one-year period is "3.5 times the amount that, at that time, is specified in column
-- 3, item 2, Table B, point 1064-B1, Pension Rate Calculator A, in the Social Security Act 1991".
-- "dependant" -- a person who "(a) ... resides with the bankrupt; (b) ... is wholly or partly dependent on the bankrupt for economic
-- support; (c) the income derived (or likely to be derived) by the person during the contribution assessment period is not more than
-- the amount prescribed". Regulations s 36: "(c) if the period begins in the financial year beginning on 1 July 2020 -- $3,741; or (d)
-- if the period begins in a later financial year -- $3,741 indexed in accordance with section 114".
@export Does this person count as my dependant for income contributions (s 139K, Regulations s 36)?
GIVEN `lives with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person lives with you
      `depends on me for economic support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person depends wholly or partly on you for economic support
      `their income in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc The person's income in the contribution assessment period, in dollars
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The Regulations s 36 amount for the period ($3,741 for a period beginning in 2020-21, indexed after that)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my dependant` IF
    `lives with me` AND `depends on me for economic support` AND `their income in the period` AT MOST `the prescribed amount`

GIVEN `the Social Security Act rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base income threshold amount` MEANS 3.5 TIMES `the Social Security Act rate`

@export What is my actual income threshold amount for a year of bankruptcy (s 139K)?
GIVEN `base threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The base income threshold amount for a one-year period, in dollars (3.5 times the Social Security Act point 1064-B1 Table B item 2 rate)
      `number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants you have
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my actual income threshold amount` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `number of dependants` AT MOST 0 THEN `base threshold`
        IF `number of dependants` EQUALS 1 THEN `base threshold` TIMES 118 DIVIDED BY 100
        IF `number of dependants` EQUALS 2 THEN `base threshold` TIMES 127 DIVIDED BY 100
        IF `number of dependants` EQUALS 3 THEN `base threshold` TIMES 132 DIVIDED BY 100
        IF `number of dependants` EQUALS 4 THEN `base threshold` TIMES 134 DIVIDED BY 100
        OTHERWISE `base threshold` TIMES 136 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 139P(1): if assessed income "exceeds the actual income threshold amount ... the bankrupt is liable to pay to the trustee a
-- contribution"; (2): if not, the bankrupt "is not liable to, but may if he or she so wishes, pay". s 139Q: a subsequent assessment
-- substitutes its own answer. s 139R: the liability survives discharge.
@export If I were bankrupt, would I have to pay an income contribution for the year (s 139P)?
GIVEN `assessed income` IS A NUMBER @desc The income your trustee assesses you are likely to derive in the year, in dollars
      `base threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The base income threshold amount for a one-year period, in dollars
      `number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants you have
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would I have to pay an income contribution` IF
    `assessed income` GREATER THAN `What is my actual income threshold amount` `base threshold` `number of dependants`

-- The amount of the contribution is set by the s 139S formula, which is missing from the deposit. This gives only the excess over the
-- threshold on which that formula works ("Assessed income" and "Actual income threshold amount" are the formula's named terms).
@export By how much would my income exceed my actual income threshold amount (the base of the s 139S contribution)?
GIVEN `assessed income` IS A NUMBER @desc The income your trustee assesses you are likely to derive in the year, in dollars
      `base threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The base income threshold amount for a one-year period, in dollars
      `number of dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependants you have
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much does my income exceed the threshold` IS
    IF `Would I have to pay an income contribution` `assessed income` `base threshold` `number of dependants`
    THEN `assessed income` MINUS `What is my actual income threshold amount` `base threshold` `number of dependants`
    ELSE 0
